go2rtc is a camera streaming application with support for a wide range
of protocols and formats, including RTSP, RTMP, WebRTC, HLS, MJPEG,
MP4 and MPEG-TS.

It can receive streams from cameras and other sources, serve them to
browsers and media players, ingest external streams, and relay them to
streaming services.  FFmpeg can be used for transcoding when a source
codec is not supported by the client.

The package includes a web interface and an HTTP API, and can also act
as an RTSP, RTMP, WebRTC, HomeKit and ONVIF server.
